Hi Ruben,

Your background check and drug screen came back clear, so we're all set for your start as a Pipefitter on Monday. Here's what you need to know for your first day:

WHEN: Monday, July 13, 2026 - please arrive at 7:45 AM for an 8:00 AM start.

WHERE: Pacific Coast Mechanical main office, 2500 S. Grand Ave, Santa Ana, CA 92705. Park in the gravel lot on the south side of the building and check in at the front office.
From there, Ray will walk you over to the shop for safety orientation and tool issue.

WHAT TO BRING:
- Original documents for Form I-9 (one from List A, or one from List B and one from List C - a driver's license plus a Social Security card is the most common combination)
- A voided check or bank letter for direct deposit
- Your OSHA 30 card
- Steel-toe boots, long pants and a long-sleeve shirt; we'll issue your hard hat, vest, gloves and safety glasses

SCHEDULE: Week one is orientation and shop time (8:00 AM - 4:30 PM). You'll be assigned to a crew starting July 20.

All of your paperwork (W-4, DE 4, direct deposit authorization, handbook acknowledgment) will be completed in person Monday morning, so there's nothing to fill out ahead of time.

If anything comes up before then, call or text me at (714) 555-0161.

See you Monday!

Gloria Esparza
HR Generalist | Pacific Coast Mechanical
